PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The panel maintains unanimous consensus for Choice B (2: 488 nm). Neutrophils arrive at the tailfin injury site well ahead of macrophages, ruling out DsRed detection at 559 nm. Furthermore, due to the 48-hour chase period exceeding the physiological lifespan of larval neutrophils, the covalently bound Cy5-HaloTag probe (~630 nm) administered at 48 hpf has been cleared by cellular turnover, leaving only newly synthesized eGFP (488 nm) detectable in the newly recruited pioneer neutrophils.
}

